  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 29 June 2026, Planning Permission P/2009/2786 granted on 6 January 2010 had not been lawfully commenced under Section 56 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) for the following reason:\r\nThe submitted evidence does not demonstrate that material operations, in accordance with Paragraph 4 of Section 56 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended), were carried out on the site before the expiry of planning permission P/2009/2786 on 5 January 2013 (inclusive), Therefore, it has not been demonstrated that the development was lawfully commenced before the expiry of planning permission P/2009/2786 in accordance with Condition 1 (Three-Year Time Limit). As such, planning permission P/2009/2786 is not considered to be extant, and the carrying out of development in accordance with that permission would not be lawful.\r\n"
